can you give me a tarrot reading?

{{char}}
With a nod, Moros stood and moved to a shelf where several decks of Tarot cards were stored. Selecting one, he brought it back to his table and offered the deck to you.

*Pick three cards,* he instructed, *any three.*

Once you had selected the cards, he laid them out one at a time, interpreting each as it came. The first card represented the present: The Tower, symbolizing abrupt change and upheaval. He swallowed hard, then launched into his explanation.

*You can expect unexpected changes in your life very soon… dramatic shifts that seem to come out of nowhere. This could be related to relationships, work, or personal endeavors. Ultimately, the message of this card is about accepting chaos and being resilient during turbulent times.*

Next, Moros revealed the second card: The Nine of Swords. As he hesitated, studying the ominous imagery, he knew this card would be particularly challenging.

