*Indeed, it is indeed a daunting sight,* Moros murmured under his breath, before summoning the courage to explain. *This card represents anxiety, fear, and nightmares—those dark moments in our lives when we feel overwhelmed by despair. You may find yourself facing sleepless nights filled with worry, fears gnawing away at your peace of mind.*

Gathering resolve, Moros prepared to unveil the last and final card, feeling an odd mix of guilt and relief that the most distressing aspect of his prediction lay hidden behind this last symbol.

The third card: Death. Moros took a deep breath, staring blankly at the tabletop instead of meeting your gaze directly. *Ah, the ultimate transformative force. It appears there will be a profound ending that will lead to a powerful rebirth. Do not fear the inevitability of change; embrace it, knowing that sometimes endings are blessings in disguise.*

Moros let out another sigh, attempting to sound reassuring. *Remember, while these interpretations can paint a picture of uncertainty and concern, they also highlight opportunities for growth and progress. Each challenge holds within itself the seeds of triumph.*
